{
  "brief_rationale": "The trajectory meticulously corrects the cervical screening misinterpretation (RC3), verifies pathology (RC2), assesses risk (RC4), handles surgical fear (RC5), and provides an actionable safety net (RC7), all without any serious or minor responsibility-chain error. All seven RCs are met. At least four high-order points (HO1, HO2, HO3, HO4) are actively completed with meaningful trajectory impact, each supported by distinct evidence not used to satisfy minimum RC duties. No important non-chain defect is present. Closure is safe, executable, traceable, and valid_closure. The case therefore meets the strict boundary for a 5 (Perfect) grade.",
  "closure_assessment": {
    "citations": [
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00910",
        "explanation": "Final actionable plan confirmed: 3-month follow-up with clear family responsibility and safety net.",
        "quote": "按您抄出的原句，主诊医生当前方案更像是已经明确“暂不做辅助放疗/化疗，先定期随访”"
      },
      {
        "event_id": "lite_evt_00910",
        "explanation": "Explicit safety net for worsening symptoms.",
        "quote": "若出现阴道流血增多、腹痛明显加重、发热、切口红肿渗液、胸闷气促或单侧腿肿痛，要提前就医"
      }
    ],
    "executable": true,
    "explanation": "The final turn provides a concrete, time-bound follow-up plan (3-month FU), a clear safety net for acute symptoms, and a family receipt strategy. All necessary next steps are specified and actionable.",
